;; FH-DIAG-003 — the compiled manifest publishes the compile-tier finding
;; roster, and a finding is governed as a FINDING rather than as a site.
;;
;; `:diagnostics` is the one manifest roster whose entries are not lexical
;; sites. The others are NAMED here rather than counted, because a tally goes
;; wrong the moment a roster arrives or leaves and a name cannot:
;; `:subscriptions` (a `sub`), `:events` (an event handler), `:slots` (a slot),
;; `:html-sites` (a `v/html`) and `:crossings` (a view crossing) each name a form
;; the compiler READ, and so own the `{:file :line :column}` source coordinate
;; FH-STRUCT-010 makes total over them. `:frame-ops` was a sixth roster until
;; rf2-h1ae3. A finding is MINTED from a node instead: it names the node's `:tag` and
;; the deterministic `:path` that reaches it, plus the compiler-minted stable
;; `:sid` its printed warning quotes. Those three are what locate it, and this
;; fixture governs that shape rather than bending a finding into the site law —
;; a synthetic coordinate on a finding would satisfy the other row and mean
;; nothing.
;;
;; The roster matters most where it is SILENT. A suppressed finding prints
;; nothing — that is what suppression is — so the manifest entry carrying the
;; author's `:reason` is its only trace, and a codebase's waivers are readable
;; from nowhere else (`004D §Compile-tier warnings`: "A suppressed finding
;; remains a manifest fact carrying its reason"). `:suppressed-keys` therefore
;; pins the conditional half of the entry shape: `:reason` rides a suppressed
;; entry and rides no other, so neither a lost reason nor a reason invented for
;; a finding nobody waived can pass.
;;
;; `:findings` is the census, and it is TOTAL: each declaration's whole roster,
;; in source order, with every hand-writable field of every entry. A count would
;; leave the contents unasserted and a per-entry key contract asserted over an
;; empty roster passes loudest of all, so the census carries all three cases the
;; law distinguishes —
;;
;;   :clean-panel          no finding at all, so the roster is EMPTY rather than
;;                         absent: "this declaration is clean" is a positive
;;                         claim, and absence would be silence a reader could
;;                         not tell from a manifest that predates the roster.
;;   :waived-drag-surface  one SUPPRESSED finding, carrying its reason. Silent
;;                         on stderr; visible only here.
;;   :unnamed-icon-button  one REPORTED finding, carrying no reason. This is the
;;                         arm that also prints, and its presence is what stops
;;                         the suppressed row above from being the only shape
;;                         the census ever inspects.
;;
;; `:sid` is the one field the census does not pin: it is a content digest the
;; compiler mints, so a fixture literal would be a copy of the implementation
;; rather than a statement about it. The suite pins its SHAPE — a non-blank
;; string — and `004D §Compile-tier warnings` owns the promise that the build
;; log and the manifest quote the same one.
{:fh/id "FH-DIAG-003"
 :required-keys   #{:sid :id :tag :path :suppressed?}
 :suppressed-keys #{:reason}
 :findings
 {:clean-panel []
  :waived-drag-surface
  [{:id          :rf.ui.compile/a11y-click-non-interactive
    :tag         :div
    :path        [0]
    :suppressed? true
    :reason      "drag surface; the keyboard path is the toolbar button"}]
  :unnamed-icon-button
  [{:id          :rf.ui.compile/a11y-missing-accessible-name
    :tag         :button
    :path        []
    :suppressed? false}]}}
